,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,3838,374,279,2629,315,678,315,279,65060,315,220,22,1948,220,16,15,15,323,220,17,15,15,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nWhat is the sum of all of the multiples of 7 between 100 and 200?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"b2730ca933b445d689dc602f95e863e43782416b6afa4ef036963997c90f90f3"},"seconds":47.400426387786865,"seed":250750233396576948,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem of finding the sum of all multiples of 7 between 100 and 200, we follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the multiples of 7 in the specified range:**\n   - The smallest multiple of 7 greater than or equal to 100 is found by dividing 100 by 7 and rounding up to the nearest whole number.\n   \\[\n   \\frac{100}{7} \\approx 14.2857 \\implies \\lceil 14.2857 \\rceil = 15\n   \\]\n   - Therefore, the smallest multiple of 7 in the range is \\( 15 \\times 7 = 105 \\).\n\n   - The largest multiple of 7 less than or equal to 200 is found by dividing 200 by 7 and rounding down to the nearest whole number.\n   \\[\n   \\frac{200}{7} \\approx 28.5714 \\implies \\lfloor 28.5714 \\rfloor = 28\n   \\]\n   - Therefore, the largest multiple of 7 in the range is \\( 28 \\times 7 = 196 \\).\n\n2. **Formulate the sequence of multiples:**\n   - The multiples of 7 between 100 and 200 form an arithmetic sequence:\n     \\[\n     105, 112, 119, \\ldots, 196\n     \\]\n   - This sequence starts at 105 and ends at 196, with a common difference of 7.\n\n3. **Determine the number of terms in the sequence:**\n   - The general term of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n     \\[\n     a_n = a + (n-1)d\n     \\]\n     where \\( a = 105 \\), \\( d = 7 \\), and \\( a_n = 196 \\).\n   - Solving for \\( n \\):\n     \\[\n     196 = 105 + (n-1) \\times 7\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     196 - 105 = (n-1) \\times 7\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     91 = (n-1) \\times 7\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     n-1 = 13\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     n = 14\n     \\]\n   - There are 14 terms in the sequence.\n\n4. **Calculate the sum of the arithmetic sequence:**\n   - The sum \\( S_n \\) of the first \\( n \\) terms of an arithmetic sequence is given by:\n     \\[\n     S_n = \\frac{n}{2} \\times (a + l)\n     \\]\n     where \\( n = 14 \\), \\( a = 105 \\), and \\( l = 196 \\).\n   - Plugging in the values:\n     \\[\n     S_{14} = \\frac{14}{2} \\times (105 + 196)\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     S_{14} = 7 \\times 301\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     S_{14} = 2107\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of all multiples of 7 between 100 and 200 is \\(\\boxed{2107}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2107}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
